/* W06.A.2 — minimal version definitions for the LD_PRELOAD shim.
 *
 * The `.symver` inline-assembly directives in src/lib.rs tag each
 * libc interposer with the version(s) FreeBSD libc actually
 * exposes for that symbol. lld refuses to emit a versioned symbol
 * unless a matching version *definition* exists in
 * `.gnu.version_d`. This script provides those definitions.
 *
 * Versions surveyed (FreeBSD 14.4 `objdump -T /lib/libc.so.7`):
 *   FBSD_1.0  — open, unlink, rename, truncate, ftruncate,
 *               pwrite, mmap, mkfifo, link, extattr_set_file,
 *               extattr_delete_file, chflags
 *   FBSD_1.1  — openat, unlinkat, renameat, mkfifoat, linkat
 *   FBSD_1.3  — chflagsat (B09; modern callers use this directly)
 *
 * Note: libc's `openat` ALSO has a `FBSD_1.2` (newer flag-aware
 * form) but lld errors with "multiple versions for openat" if
 * we emit two `.symver` directives for the same source symbol —
 * the conflict appears when the rlib gets linked into a regular
 * bin (which pulls in interposers as dead-code-but-no_mangle).
 * FBSD_1.1 covers the overwhelming majority of base-binary
 * callers; FBSD_1.2-exclusive callers fall through to libc.
 *
 * Empty bodies (`{ };`) declare each version name without
 * listing symbols. rustc auto-generates its own cdylib version
 * script (anonymous, `local: *;`) listing every `#[no_mangle]
 * pub` symbol; mixing a named body with an anonymous body
 * triggers lld's "anonymous + named version combination" error,
 * so we leave bodies empty here and let the .symver-tagged
 * symbols match the definitions by name.
 *
 * `tests/symver.rs` regression-tests that the built `.so`
 * actually exports every (symbol, version) pair we expect.
 */
FBSD_1.0 { };
FBSD_1.1 { };
FBSD_1.3 { };
